---
layout: null
search: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Search index for the caravan site.

  Regenerated by Jekyll on every build, so it always matches the live content —
  there is nothing to maintain by hand. Edit a page, run ./deploy.sh, done.

  Three sources feed this file:
    1. site.pages     — every page whose front matter does not say `search: false`
    2. site.articles  — the trip journal
    3. site.data.itinerary — one entry per caravan day, deep-linked to #day-N

  (3) exists because the itinerary page builds its 31 day cards in the browser
  from a JavaScript array. Liquid cannot see rendered output, so without this
  loop the whole trip collapsed into a single "The Itinerary" result. Both the
  page and this index now read _data/itinerary.json, so they cannot drift apart.

  Liquid's strip_html removes <script> and <style> blocks before tags, so inline
  CSS and JavaScript stay out of the index.

  Entry ids must match array position — the search page looks up docs[hit.ref] —
  so `counter` runs continuously across all three loops.

  Filters are chained rather than combined with `and`: Liquid 4.0.4, which
  GitHub Pages ships with Jekyll 3.10, cannot parse a compound expression inside
  where_exp. Newer Liquid can, so a merged condition WILL build locally and fail
  on GitHub. Verify with ./preview.sh, never the bare `jekyll` binary.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign indexed_pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.search != false" -%}
{%- assign indexed_pages = indexed_pages | where_exp: "p", "p.title" -%}
{%- assign indexed_articles = site.articles | where_exp: "a", "a.search != false" -%}
{%- assign indexed_articles = indexed_articles | where_exp: "a", "a.title" -%}
{%- assign entries = indexed_pages | concat: indexed_articles -%}
{%- assign counter = 0 -%}
[
{%- for item in entries %}
{%- if counter > 0 %},{% endif %}
  {
    "id": {{ counter }},
    "title": {{ item.title | default: "Untitled" | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ item.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
    "kind": {% if item.collection == "articles" %}"Journal"{% else %}"Page"{% endif %},
    "summary": {{ item.search_summary | default: item.hero_sub | default: item.summary | default: "" | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
    "body": {{ item.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncatewords: 700 | jsonify }}
  }
{%- assign counter = counter | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for leg in site.data.itinerary -%}
{%- for day in leg.days -%}
{%- capture day_title -%}Day {{ day.n }} · {{ day.date }} — {{ day.headline }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture day_summary -%}{{ leg.town }} · {{ leg.camp }} · {{ day.dow }}, {{ day.date }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture day_body -%}
{{ leg.town }} {{ leg.camp }} {{ day.dow }} {{ day.date }} {{ day.headline }} {{ day.heads }}
{%- for r in day.rows %} {{ r.t }} {{ r.d }}.{% endfor -%}
{%- if forloop.first and leg.travel %} {{ leg.travel.lead }} {{ leg.travel.dist }}{% for n in leg.travel.notes %} {{ n }}.{% endfor %}{% endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
,
  {
    "id": {{ counter }},
    "title": {{ day_title | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ "/itinerary/" | relative_url | append: "#day-" | append: day.n | jsonify }},
    "kind": "Itinerary",
    "summary": {{ day_summary | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
    "body": {{ day_body | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }}
  }
{%- assign counter = counter | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor %}
]
